"""Discount and tax. A phone costs Rs 15,000. 
Apply a 10% discount, then add 18% tax to the
 discounted price, and print the final price.
  Now do it the other way round: tax first, 
  then the discount. Do you get the same answer? 
  Write a comment in your code explaining why or why not"""



price = 15000
discount_rate = 10 / 100
tax_rate = 18 / 100

# Method 1: Pehle discount, phir tax
discounted_price = price * (1 - discount_rate)
final_price1 = discounted_price * (1 + tax_rate)

print("Discount first:", final_price1)

# Method 2: Pehle tax, phir discount
price_with_tax = price * (1 + tax_rate)
final_price2 = price_with_tax * (1 - discount_rate)

print("Tax first:", final_price2)

# Both give the same result because multiplying by
# the discount factor and tax factor can be done in either order.
